    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3406"
                            type="person">Mr. John Marshall</rs>
                        <lb/>The Rockefeller Foundation <lb/>49 West 49 Street <lb/><rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs> 20, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">N. Y.</rs></fw><dateline><date
                            when="1946-03-28">March 28, 1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__3406" type="person">Mr. Marshall</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>As I understand you represent for the time being <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3324" type="person">Mr. Stevens</rs> in the
                    Humanities of the Rockefeller Foundation. I write you in behalf of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1262" type="person">Prof. Siegfried Marck</rs> and
                    his manuscript about which <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3324" type="person">Mr.
                        Stevens</rs> asked me to give a report. I have talked to him before he left
                    for the West coast, and I have recommended the book which I think has a very
                    high scholarly quality. I remember that <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3324"
                        type="person">Mr. Stevens</rs> had a rather favorable reaction.</p>
                <p>I expressed at that occasion also some criticisms about the use of too much
                    German material which is not known in this country. <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1262" type="person">Prof. Marck</rs> agreed with me
                    that the sections referred to<!-- hinter <q>referred to</q> etw. gestrichen -->
                    had to be changed in order to make the book more
                    readable<!-- eigentlich <q>readible</q> --> for the American public. I would
                    like to know whether he can expect a financial help for a translator. Since the
                    voyage of <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3324" type="person">Mr. Stevens</rs> has
                    delayed the matter for several months I would be grateful to you if you gave <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1262" type="person">Prof. Marck</rs> a green signal
                    that he can go ahead with the translation.</p>
                <closer><salute>Yours sincerely,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Prof. Paul Tillich</rs>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
